From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] composefs: count only missing layers in the space check

The native composefs backend refused an upgrade unless the whole image fit
in the free space, although composefs-oci stores each layer once under its
diff id and fetches only the layers it lacks. An image sharing most layers
with the booted one (or with an attempt that was cut short) was refused
for want of space it would never use. Sum the compressed sizes of the
layers whose `oci-layer-<diff id>` stream the repository does not hold.
---
diff --git a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/switch.rs b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/switch.rs
index 0cb0b9e..fd1616c 100644
--- a/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/switch.rs
+++ b/crates/lib/src/bootc_composefs/switch.rs
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ pub(crate) async fn switch_composefs(
                     &host,
                     &target_imgref,
                     &do_upgrade_opts,
-                    &img_config.manifest,
+                    &img_config,
                 )
                 .await;
             }
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ pub(crate) async fn switch_composefs(
         &host,
         &target_imgref,
         &do_upgrade_opts,
-        &img_config.manifest,
+        &img_config,
     )
     .await?;
 
